{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"issue-1948-keyed-multiset-identity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Issue #1948: keyed MultiSet identity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0641a0e2c8a0b6c7351162f667a2eca7662ca4cd"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe unchanged production baseline was "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c879ba6d855914e5c0cac49af7a007eb5cabe7e4"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe baseline code in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db-ivm/src/{multiset,utils}.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" is also identical\nto the local main checkout at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c0d123b8"},{"type":"text","value":", used for the isolated object probe."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"contract-and-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contract and boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MultiSet.consolidate()"},{"type":"text","value":" promises that keyed records merge only when their\nkeys and values have the documented identity. String and numeric keys are\ndifferent. Primitive values compare by value; objects and functions compare\nby reference, and distinct symbols remain distinct. A two-element value is a\njoin tuple whose elements follow that leaf rule. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"consolidate()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns,\nthe complete output must retain each nonzero identity with its summed weight\nand first record. The input must remain unchanged. The oracle does not assert\noutput order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This record closes the reported direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MultiSet"},{"type":"text","value":" collisions for the oracle's\nbounded key/value grammar. It does not establish which "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" queries\nproduce primitive keyed relation values or mixed-type source keys. A live-query\nproduction witness is still needed for those application paths; the coverage\nmap names that gap."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"red-and-green-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RED and GREEN evidence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The old oracle excluded cross-type, delimiter, symbol, and function cases, so\nit remained green on the faulty implementation. The expanded oracle uses the\nsame independent reference model for eight pinned collision cases and for a\ngenerated collision branch. Before the production change:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eight pinned cases failed at multiplicity or missing-identity assertions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both generated campaigns failed. The fixed seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026929"},{"type":"text","value":" shrank to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path: \"1:0\""},{"type":"text","value":", numeric and string keys with opposite weights. Direct replay\nreached the same missing-identity assertion."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An isolated process probe with a direct object and an object tuple under\na delimiter-bearing key returned zero records. The two distinct records\nhave weights "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":" under the contract."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0641a0e2"},{"type":"text","value":", the oracle passes all 22 tests. The exact fixed seed and path\nreplay passes. The same object/tuple process probe returns two records with\nweights "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[1, -1]"},{"type":"text","value":". All 649 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db-ivm"},{"type":"text","value":" tests pass, package TypeScript\ntypechecking passes, Prettier passes, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff --check"},{"type":"text","value":" passes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original production code is the hostile wrong design for this oracle:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"str_${String(value)}"},{"type":"text","value":" erases primitive type and reference identity, and bare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"|"},{"type":"text","value":" joins erase component boundaries. Its failures reached the intended\npublic-result comparison. The repair type-tags primitive identities, uses a\nper-consolidation reference map, distinguishes a leaf from a tuple, and\nlength-prefixes components. Positive controls keep same-symbol,\nsame-function, signed-zero-key, and NaN-value merging intact."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production code changes by +10 net lines. Test code grows to make the new\ngrammar, named cases, and controls visible. No elapsed-time performance claim\nis made for the repaired hot path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"oracle-guide-audit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Oracle guide audit"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome at reviewed revision"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The oracle's opening contract cites "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MultiSet.consolidate()"},{"type":"text","value":" and limits the result to its direct API and bounded grammar."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The expected identity uses a type-tagged structured key and a local reference map. It does not call production "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getStringId"},{"type":"text","value":" or hash."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contract, model, history grammar, production call, and refinement check remain separate in the oracle file."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eight named cases reconstruct the reported regimes. The collision branch varies case and nonzero sign/magnitude; ordinary keyed histories vary record count and values. The fallback branch deliberately retains its original structural domain. A non-keyed record makes the keyed rule inapplicable."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The driver calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new MultiSet(records).consolidate().getInner()"},{"type":"text","value":" and compares every output identity, weight, and retained first record after return. The fixed campaign's reach witness covers every grammar mode."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unchanged production failed at the intended assertions; the object/tuple process probe also failed before the repair and passed after it."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same property, grammar, check, and 300-run budget execute with fixed seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026929"},{"type":"text","value":" and a seedless random campaign. Seed-plus-path replay was checked RED and GREEN. No "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fc.commands"},{"type":"text","value":" are used."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable: the reference is stateless recomputation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyedCollision"},{"type":"text","value":" is documented as a grammar branch for the same keyed production path; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"caseName"},{"type":"text","value":" is only a replay label."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No external resources are acquired. Shrinking and direct replay preserve the missing-identity failure at the result checkpoint."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No separate shared semantic fault was named. The reference's structured key differs from production's length-prefixed composition, and the positive controls challenge adjacent identity equivalences."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This versioned record identifies the exact executable revision, RED/GREEN receipts, limits, and the outcomes above."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pr-1967-external-review-follow-up","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR #1967 external-review follow-up"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b39e162f82bfc8b228841970b0c31bd5624b508f"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe review targeted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bd0a95eaa39c5b99ae420752de3b5f100b4cd183"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe production encoder did not change in this follow-up."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new pinned witness uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NaN"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" as numeric keys.\nBefore the model repair, the witness failed at the multiplicity assertion.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":" converted all three raw numeric keys to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":", so the model\nexpected one group with weight 6. Production returned three distinct groups.\nThe repaired model compares keys and leaves directly with SameValueZero, then\ncompares the two elements of join tuples. It does not serialize keyed identity.\nThe keyed generator now includes all three non-finite keys. The unkeyed\nstructural fallback retains its former key and value domains."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same focused witness is GREEN after the model repair. All 23 consolidation\noracle tests, all 650 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db-ivm"},{"type":"text","value":" tests, package typechecking, Prettier,\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff --check"},{"type":"text","value":" pass. The full package run disabled coverage output.\nThe old production files from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c879ba6d"},{"type":"text","value":" were run with the new oracle in an\nisolated directory. The numeric/string-key witness failed at the public\nmultiplicity comparison: production returned weight 2 where the model required\nweight 1. A bigint/number value witness failed at the missing-identity\ncomparison. An initial isolated run stopped during TypeScript configuration\nsetup; that run is not counted as a mutant kill. The reruns reached the\nassertions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The external review also questioned the baseline label. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c879ba6d"},{"type":"text","value":" was the\nrecorded unchanged production baseline. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c0d123b8"},{"type":"text","value":" was its child and supplied\nthe isolated object probe. Both commits have identical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"multiset.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"utils.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" blobs. The coverage map's RED baseline is accurate."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Follow-up outcome at reviewed revision"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-001"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The keyed law and direct-API limit remain in the opening contract. It now names non-finite keys in the grammar."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-002"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct SameValueZero/reference equality supplies expected keyed groups. It does not use production's string encoding or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getStringId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-003"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contract, model, grammar, production call, and result comparison remain visible in one file."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-004"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pinned non-finite-key case reconstructs the false RED. The keyed generator adds those keys; the fallback generator keeps its prior domains. The earlier collision reconstruction and exclusions remain."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-005"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The driver still calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MultiSet.consolidate()"},{"type":"text","value":" and compares every output group, weight, and retained first record after return."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-006"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The unchanged pre-fix encoder fails the revised model at the intended public-result assertion. Setup failure was not credited."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-007"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed and seedless 300-run campaigns retain the same grammar and comparison within each revision. Seed-plus-path replay support remains."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-008"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not applicable: the model is stateless recomputation."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-009"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyedCollision"},{"type":"text","value":" grammar branch and replay label retain their declared mapping."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-010"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No external resources are acquired. The isolated baseline rerun reached the same result checkpoint."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-011"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A shared type/text encoding concern now has a second formulation: direct SameValueZero/reference equality. The old encoder fails it."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ORC-012"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This append-only entry records the revised executable commit, false-RED repair, hostile baseline, GREEN checks, and limits."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct replay also used fixed seed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026929"},{"type":"text","value":" and shrink path "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1:0"},{"type":"text","value":" with the\nrevised model. The old encoder failed after one replay case at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"missing identities"},{"type":"text","value":", with numeric and string keys carrying opposite weights. The same\nseed and path passed on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b39e162f"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"issue-1948-keyed-multiset-identity","text":"Issue #1948: keyed MultiSet identity","level":1},{"id":"contract-and-boundary","text":"Contract and boundary","level":2},{"id":"red-and-green-evidence","text":"RED and GREEN evidence","level":2},{"id":"oracle-guide-audit","text":"Oracle guide audit","level":2},{"id":"pr-1967-external-review-follow-up","text":"PR #1967 external-review follow-up","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Issue #1948: keyed MultiSet identity\n\nReviewed executable revision: `0641a0e2c8a0b6c7351162f667a2eca7662ca4cd`.\nThe unchanged production baseline was `c879ba6d855914e5c0cac49af7a007eb5cabe7e4`.\nThe baseline code in `packages/db-ivm/src/{multiset,utils}.ts` is also identical\nto the local main checkout at `c0d123b8`, used for the isolated object probe.\n\n## Contract and boundary\n\n`MultiSet.consolidate()` promises that keyed records merge only when their\nkeys and values have the documented identity. String and numeric keys are\ndifferent. Primitive values compare by value; objects and functions compare\nby reference, and distinct symbols remain distinct. A two-element value is a\njoin tuple whose elements follow that leaf rule. After `consolidate()` returns,\nthe complete output must retain each nonzero identity with its summed weight\nand first record. The input must remain unchanged. The oracle does not assert\noutput order.\n\nThis record closes the reported direct `MultiSet` collisions for the oracle's\nbounded key/value grammar. It does not establish which `@tanstack/db` queries\nproduce primitive keyed relation values or mixed-type source keys. A live-query\nproduction witness is still needed for those application paths; the coverage\nmap names that gap.\n\n## RED and GREEN evidence\n\nThe old oracle excluded cross-type, delimiter, symbol, and function cases, so\nit remained green on the faulty implementation. The expanded oracle uses the\nsame independent reference model for eight pinned collision cases and for a\ngenerated collision branch. Before the production change:\n\n- Eight pinned cases failed at multiplicity or missing-identity assertions.\n- Both generated campaigns failed. The fixed seed `2026929` shrank to\n  `path: \"1:0\"`, numeric and string keys with opposite weights. Direct replay\n  reached the same missing-identity assertion.\n- An isolated process probe with a direct object and an object tuple under\n  a delimiter-bearing key returned zero records. The two distinct records\n  have weights `1` and `-1` under the contract.\n\nOn `0641a0e2`, the oracle passes all 22 tests. The exact fixed seed and path\nreplay passes. The same object/tuple process probe returns two records with\nweights `[1, -1]`. All 649 `@tanstack/db-ivm` tests pass, package TypeScript\ntypechecking passes, Prettier passes, and `git diff --check` passes.\n\nThe original production code is the hostile wrong design for this oracle:\n`str_${String(value)}` erases primitive type and reference identity, and bare\n`|` joins erase component boundaries. Its failures reached the intended\npublic-result comparison. The repair type-tags primitive identities, uses a\nper-consolidation reference map, distinguishes a leaf from a tuple, and\nlength-prefixes components. Positive controls keep same-symbol,\nsame-function, signed-zero-key, and NaN-value merging intact.\n\nProduction code changes by +10 net lines. Test code grows to make the new\ngrammar, named cases, and controls visible. No elapsed-time performance claim\nis made for the repaired hot path.\n\n## Oracle guide audit\n\n| Requirement | Outcome at reviewed revision |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The oracle's opening contract cites `MultiSet.consolidate()` and limits the result to its direct API and bounded grammar. |\n| ORC-002 | The expected identity uses a type-tagged structured key and a local reference map. It does not call production `getStringId` or hash. |\n| ORC-003 | Contract, model, history grammar, production call, and refinement check remain separate in the oracle file. |\n| ORC-004 | Eight named cases reconstruct the reported regimes. The collision branch varies case and nonzero sign/magnitude; ordinary keyed histories vary record count and values. The fallback branch deliberately retains its original structural domain. A non-keyed record makes the keyed rule inapplicable. |\n| ORC-005 | The driver calls `new MultiSet(records).consolidate().getInner()` and compares every output identity, weight, and retained first record after return. The fixed campaign's reach witness covers every grammar mode. |\n| ORC-006 | Unchanged production failed at the intended assertions; the object/tuple process probe also failed before the repair and passed after it. |\n| ORC-007 | The same property, grammar, check, and 300-run budget execute with fixed seed `2026929` and a seedless random campaign. Seed-plus-path replay was checked RED and GREEN. No `fc.commands` are used. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable: the reference is stateless recomputation. |\n| ORC-009 | `keyedCollision` is documented as a grammar branch for the same keyed production path; `caseName` is only a replay label. |\n| ORC-010 | No external resources are acquired. Shrinking and direct replay preserve the missing-identity failure at the result checkpoint. |\n| ORC-011 | No separate shared semantic fault was named. The reference's structured key differs from production's length-prefixed composition, and the positive controls challenge adjacent identity equivalences. |\n| ORC-012 | This versioned record identifies the exact executable revision, RED/GREEN receipts, limits, and the outcomes above. |\n\n## PR #1967 external-review follow-up\n\nReviewed executable revision: `b39e162f82bfc8b228841970b0c31bd5624b508f`.\nThe review targeted `bd0a95eaa39c5b99ae420752de3b5f100b4cd183`.\nThe production encoder did not change in this follow-up.\n\nA new pinned witness uses `NaN`, `Infinity`, and `-Infinity` as numeric keys.\nBefore the model repair, the witness failed at the multiplicity assertion.\n`JSON.stringify` converted all three raw numeric keys to `null`, so the model\nexpected one group with weight 6. Production returned three distinct groups.\nThe repaired model compares keys and leaves directly with SameValueZero, then\ncompares the two elements of join tuples. It does not serialize keyed identity.\nThe keyed generator now includes all three non-finite keys. The unkeyed\nstructural fallback retains its former key and value domains.\n\nThe same focused witness is GREEN after the model repair. All 23 consolidation\noracle tests, all 650 `@tanstack/db-ivm` tests, package typechecking, Prettier,\nand `git diff --check` pass. The full package run disabled coverage output.\nThe old production files from `c879ba6d` were run with the new oracle in an\nisolated directory. The numeric/string-key witness failed at the public\nmultiplicity comparison: production returned weight 2 where the model required\nweight 1. A bigint/number value witness failed at the missing-identity\ncomparison. An initial isolated run stopped during TypeScript configuration\nsetup; that run is not counted as a mutant kill. The reruns reached the\nassertions.\n\nThe external review also questioned the baseline label. `c879ba6d` was the\nrecorded unchanged production baseline. `c0d123b8` was its child and supplied\nthe isolated object probe. Both commits have identical `multiset.ts` and\n`utils.ts` blobs. The coverage map's RED baseline is accurate.\n\n| Requirement | Follow-up outcome at reviewed revision |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The keyed law and direct-API limit remain in the opening contract. It now names non-finite keys in the grammar. |\n| ORC-002 | Direct SameValueZero/reference equality supplies expected keyed groups. It does not use production's string encoding or `getStringId`. |\n| ORC-003 | Contract, model, grammar, production call, and result comparison remain visible in one file. |\n| ORC-004 | The pinned non-finite-key case reconstructs the false RED. The keyed generator adds those keys; the fallback generator keeps its prior domains. The earlier collision reconstruction and exclusions remain. |\n| ORC-005 | The driver still calls `MultiSet.consolidate()` and compares every output group, weight, and retained first record after return. |\n| ORC-006 | The unchanged pre-fix encoder fails the revised model at the intended public-result assertion. Setup failure was not credited. |\n| ORC-007 | Fixed and seedless 300-run campaigns retain the same grammar and comparison within each revision. Seed-plus-path replay support remains. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable: the model is stateless recomputation. |\n| ORC-009 | The `keyedCollision` grammar branch and replay label retain their declared mapping. |\n| ORC-010 | No external resources are acquired. The isolated baseline rerun reached the same result checkpoint. |\n| ORC-011 | A shared type/text encoding concern now has a second formulation: direct SameValueZero/reference equality. The old encoder fails it. |\n| ORC-012 | This append-only entry records the revised executable commit, false-RED repair, hostile baseline, GREEN checks, and limits. |\n\nDirect replay also used fixed seed `2026929` and shrink path `1:0` with the\nrevised model. The old encoder failed after one replay case at `missing\nidentities`, with numeric and string keys carrying opposite weights. The same\nseed and path passed on `b39e162f`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Issue #1948: keyed MultiSet identity\n\nReviewed executable revision: `0641a0e2c8a0b6c7351162f667a2eca7662ca4cd`.\nThe unchanged production baseline was `c879ba6d855914e5c0cac49af7a007eb5cabe7e4`.\nThe baseline code in `packages/db-ivm/src/{multiset,utils}.ts` is also identical\nto the local main checkout at `c0d123b8`, used for the isolated object probe.\n\n## Contract and boundary\n\n`MultiSet.consolidate()` promises that keyed records merge only when their\nkeys and values have the documented identity. String and numeric keys are\ndifferent. Primitive values compare by value; objects and functions compare\nby reference, and distinct symbols remain distinct. A two-element value is a\njoin tuple whose elements follow that leaf rule. After `consolidate()` returns,\nthe complete output must retain each nonzero identity with its summed weight\nand first record. The input must remain unchanged. The oracle does not assert\noutput order.\n\nThis record closes the reported direct `MultiSet` collisions for the oracle's\nbounded key/value grammar. It does not establish which `@tanstack/db` queries\nproduce primitive keyed relation values or mixed-type source keys. A live-query\nproduction witness is still needed for those application paths; the coverage\nmap names that gap.\n\n## RED and GREEN evidence\n\nThe old oracle excluded cross-type, delimiter, symbol, and function cases, so\nit remained green on the faulty implementation. The expanded oracle uses the\nsame independent reference model for eight pinned collision cases and for a\ngenerated collision branch. Before the production change:\n\n- Eight pinned cases failed at multiplicity or missing-identity assertions.\n- Both generated campaigns failed. The fixed seed `2026929` shrank to\n  `path: \"1:0\"`, numeric and string keys with opposite weights. Direct replay\n  reached the same missing-identity assertion.\n- An isolated process probe with a direct object and an object tuple under\n  a delimiter-bearing key returned zero records. The two distinct records\n  have weights `1` and `-1` under the contract.\n\nOn `0641a0e2`, the oracle passes all 22 tests. The exact fixed seed and path\nreplay passes. The same object/tuple process probe returns two records with\nweights `[1, -1]`. All 649 `@tanstack/db-ivm` tests pass, package TypeScript\ntypechecking passes, Prettier passes, and `git diff --check` passes.\n\nThe original production code is the hostile wrong design for this oracle:\n`str_${String(value)}` erases primitive type and reference identity, and bare\n`|` joins erase component boundaries. Its failures reached the intended\npublic-result comparison. The repair type-tags primitive identities, uses a\nper-consolidation reference map, distinguishes a leaf from a tuple, and\nlength-prefixes components. Positive controls keep same-symbol,\nsame-function, signed-zero-key, and NaN-value merging intact.\n\nProduction code changes by +10 net lines. Test code grows to make the new\ngrammar, named cases, and controls visible. No elapsed-time performance claim\nis made for the repaired hot path.\n\n## Oracle guide audit\n\n| Requirement | Outcome at reviewed revision |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The oracle's opening contract cites `MultiSet.consolidate()` and limits the result to its direct API and bounded grammar. |\n| ORC-002 | The expected identity uses a type-tagged structured key and a local reference map. It does not call production `getStringId` or hash. |\n| ORC-003 | Contract, model, history grammar, production call, and refinement check remain separate in the oracle file. |\n| ORC-004 | Eight named cases reconstruct the reported regimes. The collision branch varies case and nonzero sign/magnitude; ordinary keyed histories vary record count and values. The fallback branch deliberately retains its original structural domain. A non-keyed record makes the keyed rule inapplicable. |\n| ORC-005 | The driver calls `new MultiSet(records).consolidate().getInner()` and compares every output identity, weight, and retained first record after return. The fixed campaign's reach witness covers every grammar mode. |\n| ORC-006 | Unchanged production failed at the intended assertions; the object/tuple process probe also failed before the repair and passed after it. |\n| ORC-007 | The same property, grammar, check, and 300-run budget execute with fixed seed `2026929` and a seedless random campaign. Seed-plus-path replay was checked RED and GREEN. No `fc.commands` are used. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable: the reference is stateless recomputation. |\n| ORC-009 | `keyedCollision` is documented as a grammar branch for the same keyed production path; `caseName` is only a replay label. |\n| ORC-010 | No external resources are acquired. Shrinking and direct replay preserve the missing-identity failure at the result checkpoint. |\n| ORC-011 | No separate shared semantic fault was named. The reference's structured key differs from production's length-prefixed composition, and the positive controls challenge adjacent identity equivalences. |\n| ORC-012 | This versioned record identifies the exact executable revision, RED/GREEN receipts, limits, and the outcomes above. |\n\n## PR #1967 external-review follow-up\n\nReviewed executable revision: `b39e162f82bfc8b228841970b0c31bd5624b508f`.\nThe review targeted `bd0a95eaa39c5b99ae420752de3b5f100b4cd183`.\nThe production encoder did not change in this follow-up.\n\nA new pinned witness uses `NaN`, `Infinity`, and `-Infinity` as numeric keys.\nBefore the model repair, the witness failed at the multiplicity assertion.\n`JSON.stringify` converted all three raw numeric keys to `null`, so the model\nexpected one group with weight 6. Production returned three distinct groups.\nThe repaired model compares keys and leaves directly with SameValueZero, then\ncompares the two elements of join tuples. It does not serialize keyed identity.\nThe keyed generator now includes all three non-finite keys. The unkeyed\nstructural fallback retains its former key and value domains.\n\nThe same focused witness is GREEN after the model repair. All 23 consolidation\noracle tests, all 650 `@tanstack/db-ivm` tests, package typechecking, Prettier,\nand `git diff --check` pass. The full package run disabled coverage output.\nThe old production files from `c879ba6d` were run with the new oracle in an\nisolated directory. The numeric/string-key witness failed at the public\nmultiplicity comparison: production returned weight 2 where the model required\nweight 1. A bigint/number value witness failed at the missing-identity\ncomparison. An initial isolated run stopped during TypeScript configuration\nsetup; that run is not counted as a mutant kill. The reruns reached the\nassertions.\n\nThe external review also questioned the baseline label. `c879ba6d` was the\nrecorded unchanged production baseline. `c0d123b8` was its child and supplied\nthe isolated object probe. Both commits have identical `multiset.ts` and\n`utils.ts` blobs. The coverage map's RED baseline is accurate.\n\n| Requirement | Follow-up outcome at reviewed revision |\n| --- | --- |\n| ORC-001 | The keyed law and direct-API limit remain in the opening contract. It now names non-finite keys in the grammar. |\n| ORC-002 | Direct SameValueZero/reference equality supplies expected keyed groups. It does not use production's string encoding or `getStringId`. |\n| ORC-003 | Contract, model, grammar, production call, and result comparison remain visible in one file. |\n| ORC-004 | The pinned non-finite-key case reconstructs the false RED. The keyed generator adds those keys; the fallback generator keeps its prior domains. The earlier collision reconstruction and exclusions remain. |\n| ORC-005 | The driver still calls `MultiSet.consolidate()` and compares every output group, weight, and retained first record after return. |\n| ORC-006 | The unchanged pre-fix encoder fails the revised model at the intended public-result assertion. Setup failure was not credited. |\n| ORC-007 | Fixed and seedless 300-run campaigns retain the same grammar and comparison within each revision. Seed-plus-path replay support remains. |\n| ORC-008 | Not applicable: the model is stateless recomputation. |\n| ORC-009 | The `keyedCollision` grammar branch and replay label retain their declared mapping. |\n| ORC-010 | No external resources are acquired. The isolated baseline rerun reached the same result checkpoint. |\n| ORC-011 | A shared type/text encoding concern now has a second formulation: direct SameValueZero/reference equality. The old encoder fails it. |\n| ORC-012 | This append-only entry records the revised executable commit, false-RED repair, hostile baseline, GREEN checks, and limits. |\n\nDirect replay also used fixed seed `2026929` and shrink path `1:0` with the\nrevised model. The old encoder failed after one replay case at `missing\nidentities`, with numeric and string keys carrying opposite weights. The same\nseed and path passed on `b39e162f`.\n"}
